<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIAN BOURSE POSTPONED LISTING APPROVALS.</title>
<headline>ESTONIAN BOURSE POSTPONED LISTING APPROVALS.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tallinn bourse listing commission said on Tuesday that it did not approve the listing applications of three companies and will discuss them again on July 15.</p>
<p>Construction company Merko and car dealer Fakto had applied to list their shares on the main list and Leks Insurance on the secondary list. </p>
<p>Viru Rand also applied to start trading on the free market.</p>
<p>The bourse managing director Helo Meigas told Reuters that the companies must submit additional information before their applications can be approved.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
